<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3344] Revert comments in JDBC interpreter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3344</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In Zeppelin the paragraph can contain multiple SQL queries delimeted by &apos;;&apos;.&lt;br/&gt;
The original purpose of PR2518 &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; was correct processing of &apos;;&apos;. This was done via full removing comments from code.&lt;br/&gt;
Unfortunately Apache Phoenix uses hooks in comments &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
Thus we should not delete comments in scripts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There was discussion about comment rules for different databases (solr). The right way is keep style. Thus analysts can copy queries to another tool and can get same results and errors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2158&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2158&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2279&quot; title=&quot;Incorrect parsing queries if there are comments&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2279&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2279&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; excluded comments from SQL&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://forcedotcom.github.io/phoenix/#hint&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://forcedotcom.github.io/phoenix/#hint&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
